values ('d7e8f9a0-1b2c-4e37-8f67-8a9b0c1d2e77', 'ethics-in-criminal-justice', 'Ethics in Criminal Justice', 'Ethics in Criminal Justice teaches the ethical vocabulary needed to analyze decisions across policing, courts, corrections, research, and policy when legal permission and moral justification diverge. Students examine legitimacy and procedural justice, police discretion and use of force, surveillance and privacy, bias and equal protection, misconduct and accountability, investigative and forensic integrity, prosecutorial and defense duties, judicial and pretrial ethics, correctional dignity, punishment theory, victims and restorative justice, data and algorithmic risk, and ethical leadership.');

